-- chem/rootsum.cub — √V and the holonomy trace tr M_e as exact root sums. With S = Σ ε q_IJK on a vertex's
-- invariants and Q_v = (i/4) S (Brunnemann–Thiemann eq. 9), T = Q_v² = −S²/16 is a rational matrix with
-- non-negative eigenvalues, V_v = T^{1/4} and √V_v = T^{1/8}. T is diagonalisable (Q_v is self-adjoint for
-- the invariant inner product), so with m its minimal polynomial, p/gcd(p, p′) for p its characteristic
-- polynomial, the projector onto the eigenvalue τ is (m(T)/(T − τ))/m′(τ), and m(t)/(t − τ) = Σ_k u_k(τ) t^k
-- with u_k(τ) = Σ_{i>k} m_i τ^{i−k−1}. Hence, for B_k = R T^k E (chem/holonomy.cub) and C_p = Σ_k m_{k+1+p} B_k,
--   R √V E = Σ_{m(τ)=0} τ^{1/8} (Σ_p τ^p C_p)/m′(τ),
-- and tr M_e = Σ_± ((2j_±+1)/(2j+1)) R_± √V_± E_± (Thiemann, QSD V eq. 3.8): a finite sum over the roots of
-- rational polynomials, with rational matrix coefficients. Nothing in it is chosen or approximated.
import "holonomy.cub"

